const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文在直接成本数据不可得时，利用日收益为零的发生情况估计有效交易成本。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article develops an estimate of effective transaction costs when direct cost data are unavailable, using the incidence of zero daily returns. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"模型把零收益纳入收益生成过程，仅由日收益历史产生公司、交易所和时期层面的平均往返成本估计。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"Its model places zero returns inside a return-generating process to produce firm-, exchange-, and period-level average round-trip cost estimates from daily return histories. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入包括清洗后的日收益序列、零收益定义、证券与交易所身份、样本日期、公司行动调整，以及陈旧或缺失价格过滤。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Inputs are a clean daily return series, zero-return definition, security and exchange identities, sample dates, corporate-action adjustments, and filters for stale or missing prices. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要提出基于收益的成本估计器及其与常用估计器的比较，并不把每一个零收益等同于已知执行成本。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The public abstract presents a return-based cost estimator and comparisons with commonly used estimators; it does not equate a zero return with a known execution cost for every asset. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"保留未四舍五入和复权价格规则；区分停牌、陈旧和缺失观测；记录样本资格、收益频率和成本基准比较。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Retain unrounded and adjusted price rules; distinguish suspended, stale, and missing observations; record sample eligibility, return frequency, and any benchmark-cost comparison. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (1999)。日收益代理并非观察到的买卖价差、费率表或可执行全成本，特别是在不同资产和市场结构间。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (1999). A daily-return proxy is not an observed bid-ask spread, fee schedule, or executable all-in cost, especially across different assets and market structures. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/12.5.1113",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1999) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“A New Estimate of Transaction Costs”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。日收益代理并非观察到的买卖价差、费率表或可执行全成本，特别是在不同资产和市场结构间。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “A New Estimate of Transaction Costs”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
